{"type":"output_text","text":{"value":"Here’s a comprehensive guide to using the latest `com.azure:azure-ai-agents-persistent` Java SDK (v1.0.0-beta.2 as of August 2026) for synchronous agent creation, thread management, file search, and vector store operations, focusing on practical code examples:

---

## 1. Setup Maven Dependencies

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.azure</groupId>
  <artifactId>azure-ai-agents-persistent</artifactId>
  <version>1.0.0-beta.2</version>
</dependency>
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.azure</groupId>
  <artifactId>azure-identity</artifactId>
  <version>1.14.2</version>
</dependency>
```

---

## 2. Client Initialization

```java
import com.azure.ai.agents.persistent.PersistentAgentsClient;
import com.azure.ai.agents.persistent.PersistentAgentsClientBuilder;
import com.azure.identity.DefaultAzureCredentialBuilder;

// Set up environment variables: PROJECT_ENDPOINT, MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME
String endpoint = System.getenv("PROJECT_ENDPOINT");
PersistentAgentsClient client = new PersistentAgentsClientBuilder()
    .endpoint(endpoint)
    .credential(new DefaultAzureCredentialBuilder().build())
    .buildClient();
```
---

## 3. Create an Agent

```java
import com.azure.ai.agents.persistent.models.PersistentAgent;

String modelDeploymentName = System.getenv("MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME");
PersistentAgent agent = client.createAgent(
    modelDeploymentName,
    "Math Tutor",
    "You are a personal math tutor. Help students understand math concepts."
);
System.out.printf("Agent created: %s%n", agent.getId());
```
---

## 4. Create a Thread

```java
import com.azure.ai.agents.persistent.models.PersistentAgentThread;

PersistentAgentThread thread = client.createThread();
System.out.printf("Thread created: %s%n", thread.getId());
```
---

## 5. File Search & Vector Store Example

- **Register (upload) file:** Use the Files client to upload/search.
- **Create a vector store:** Use the VectorStores client to create a new store for your document corpus.

```java
// Upload file and register (see API for details)
var filesClient = client.getFilesClient();
// File upload logic here, typically returning a fileId

// Create vector store (simple example)
var vectorStoresClient = client.getVectorStoresClient();
// Provide configuration as needed

// Now attach file search tool with files and vector store
```

---

## 6. Create Message, Run, and Poll for Completion

```java
client.createMessage(thread.getId(), "user", "Show me math examples with my uploaded file.");

// Start run (invoke agent)
var run = client.createRun(thread.getId(), agent.getId());
while (run.getStatus().isInProgress()) {
    Thread.sleep(500);
    run = client.getRun(thread.getId(), run.getId());
}

// Retrieve and print assistant's responses
client.listMessages(thread.getId()).forEach(msg ->
    System.out.println(msg.getRole() + ": " + msg.getContent())
);
```
---

